//@version=6
//@description Shared level-line, right-label, history-array, start-time, and newest-first rolling-window helpers for MYNAMEISBRANDON Pine scripts.

library("ImportantLevelsLinesLabels_Utilities", true)

// ==============================================================================================
// 🟢 REGION: Library Overview
// ==============================================================================================
//
// LevelLineLabel_Utilities is an engine-agnostic level output library.
//
// This library is designed to help MYNAMEISBRANDON scripts render horizontal price levels,
// compact right-side labels, source-aware line starts, synchronized object slots, history arrays,
// and newest-first rolling-window extremes in a consistent way across Candle Levels, VWAP Levels,
// trendline tools, envelope tools, price-pane companions, and future level-based scripts.
//
// Important design note:
//
// • This library does not request higher-timeframe data.
// • This library does not decide regular-session versus extended-session sources.
// • This library does not detect sessions, opens, closes, highs, lows, or pivots.
// • This library does not decide which levels should be shown.
// • This library does not own script inputs, tooltips, colors, or final visibility logic.
// • The calling script remains responsible for the level engine, source engine, session model,
//   request.security() calls, user inputs, colors, and final show/hide conditions.
//
// What this library provides:
//
// • Line-style and label-size resolvers
// • EM-space label padding helpers
// • Significant-figure and compact numeric formatting helpers
// • Price, money-difference, and percent-difference text helpers
// • Standard right-side level label text builder
// • Above/below-current-price color routing helper
// • Bar-time horizontal level line manager
// • Transparent right-side text label manager
// • Synchronized line/label slot-array managers
// • Float / int / line / label array pruning helpers
// • Newest-first history lookup helpers
// • Active Period / Source Window / Source Candle start-time helpers
// • Newest-first rolling highest / lowest helpers
// • Newest-first rolling highest / lowest helpers with matching source time
//
// Level label model:
//
// • Optional price row
// • Optional $ difference row
// • Optional % difference row
// • Required level tag row supplied by the calling script
// • EM-space padding is added to each row so scripts can visually stagger right-side labels
//   without offsetting label x positions away from bar_index.
//
// Start-time model:
//
// • Active Period:
//   - Uses the active period start supplied by the calling script.
//
// • Source Window:
//   - Uses the completed source window start supplied by the calling script.
//
// • Source Candle / Source Close Candle:
//   - Uses the exact source candle time supplied by the calling script when available.
//   - Falls back to Source Window when available.
//   - Falls back to Active Period when neither source time is available.
//
// Newest-first history model:
//
// • Index 0 is expected to be the most recent completed record.
// • Index 1 is one completed record back.
// • Index 2 is two completed records back.
// • Rolling helpers scan from index 0 upward and keep the most recent matching extreme on ties.
//
// Recommended usage:
//
// • Keep source/session/request logic inside the calling script.
// • Use this library after the script has already resolved level values and source times.
// • Use object slot arrays when the script has many repeated level line/label pairs.
// • Use newest-first rolling helpers when history arrays are populated with array.unshift().
// • Keep public-facing input and tooltip wording at script level.
//
// ==============================================================================================
// 🔴 END REGION: Library Overview
// ==============================================================================================


// ==============================================================================================
// 📚 LIBRARY MAP
// ==============================================================================================
//
// LevelLineLabel_Utilities is organized into:
//
// • Style Helpers
// • Text Formatting Helpers
// • Level Label Text Helpers
// • Object Sync Helpers
// • Slot Array Helpers
// • History Array Helpers
// • Source Start-Time Helpers
// • Newest-First Rolling Extreme Helpers
//
// ==============================================================================================


// ==============================================================================================
// 🟢 REGION: Style Helpers
// ==============================================================================================
//
// 📌 PURPOSE:
//     Provides reusable style resolvers for level-line and right-label scripts.
//
// 🧠 USER-FACING MODEL:
//     These helpers convert simple UI strings into Pine style enums so scripts can keep
//     input wording consistent while centralizing style translation.
//

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Line Style Resolver
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────

// @function Resolves a Pine line style from a user-facing string.
// @param styleIn Style string. Expected values: "Solid", "Dashed", or "Dotted".
// @returns Pine line style enum.
export levelLineStyle(simple string styleIn) =>
    styleIn == "Solid" ? line.style_solid :
     styleIn == "Dashed" ? line.style_dashed : line.style_dotted

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Label Size Resolver
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────

// @function Resolves a Pine label size from a user-facing string.
// @param sizeIn Size string. Expected values: "Tiny", "Small", "Normal", "Large", or "Huge".
// @returns Pine label size enum.
export levelLabelSize(simple string sizeIn) =>
    sizeIn == "Tiny" ? size.tiny :
     sizeIn == "Small" ? size.small :
     sizeIn == "Large" ? size.large :
     sizeIn == "Huge" ? size.huge : size.normal

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Above / Below Price Color Resolver
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────

// @function Resolves a color from whether current price is above or below a level.
// @param level Level price.
// @param currentPrice Current/reference price used for comparison.
// @param aboveColor Color returned when currentPrice is greater than or equal to level.
// @param belowColor Color returned when currentPrice is below level.
// @returns Resolved color.
export levelColor(
     float level,
     float currentPrice,
     color aboveColor,
     color belowColor) =>

    not na(level) and not na(currentPrice) and currentPrice >= level ? aboveColor : belowColor

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Example Usage
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Example:
//
// import MYNAMEISBRANDON/LevelLineLabel_Utilities/1 as LVL
//
// string lineStyle = LVL.levelLineStyle("Dotted")
// string labelSize = LVL.levelLabelSize("Normal")
// color levelCol = LVL.levelColor(prevHigh, close, color.yellow, color.red)
//
// ==============================================================================================
// 🔴 END REGION: Style Helpers
// ==============================================================================================


// ==============================================================================================
// 🟢 REGION: Text Formatting Helpers
// ==============================================================================================
//
// 📌 PURPOSE:
//     Provides label-safe numeric formatting helpers for level values, money differences,
//     percent differences, and EM-space label padding.
//
// 🧠 USER-FACING MODEL:
//     These helpers keep right-side labels compact and readable across high-priced stocks,
//     low-priced stocks, crypto pairs, futures-style symbols, and other price scales.
//

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: EM-Space Spacer
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────

// @function Builds an EM-space spacer for right-side text labels.
// @param pad Number of EM spaces. Values are clamped from 0 to 100.
// @returns Spacer string.
export levelSpacer(int pad) =>
    str.repeat(" ", math.min(math.max(pad, 0), 100))

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Trailing-Zero Trimmer
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────

// @function Removes trailing zeros and a trailing decimal point from formatted numeric text.
// @param txt Numeric text.
// @returns Trimmed numeric text.
export levelTrimTrailingZeros(string txt) =>
    string out = txt

    if str.contains(out, ".")
        while str.length(out) > 0 and str.substring(out, str.length(out) - 1, str.length(out)) == "0"
            out := str.substring(out, 0, str.length(out) - 1)

        if str.length(out) > 0 and str.substring(out, str.length(out) - 1, str.length(out)) == "."
            out := str.substring(out, 0, str.length(out) - 1)

    out

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Leading-Zero Trimmer
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────

// @function Removes the leading zero from decimals such as 0.42 or -0.42.
// @param txt Numeric text.
// @returns Numeric text with leading decimal zero removed when applicable.
export levelStripLeadingZero(string txt) =>
    string out = txt
    int len = str.length(out)

    if len >= 2 and str.substring(out, 0, 2) == "0."
        out := str.substring(out, 1, len)
    else if len >= 3 and str.substring(out, 0, 3) == "-0."
        out := "-" + str.substring(out, 2, len)

    out

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Significant-Figure Resolver
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────

// @function Rounds a value to a requested number of significant figures.
// @param value Value to round.
// @param figs Significant figures.
// @returns Rounded value.
export levelSigFig(
     float value,
     int figs) =>

    float out = value

    if not na(value) and value != 0.0
        int safeFigs = math.max(figs, 1)
        float digits = math.floor(math.log(math.abs(value)) / math.log(10))
        float factor = math.pow(10, safeFigs - 1 - digits)
        out := math.round(value * factor) / factor

    out

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Generic Number Text Formatter
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────

// @function Formats a number with a supplied Pine format pattern, then trims trailing and leading zeros.
// @param value Value to format.
// @param pattern str.tostring() numeric pattern.
// @returns Formatted number text, or n/a when value is na.
export levelNumberText(
     float value,
     simple string pattern) =>

    na(value) ? "n/a" : levelStripLeadingZero(levelTrimTrailingZeros(str.tostring(value, pattern)))

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Price Text Formatter
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────

// @function Formats a level price using significant figures and compact decimal trimming.
// @param value Price value.
// @param sigFigs Significant figures.
// @returns Formatted price text.
export levelPriceText(
     float value,
     simple int sigFigs) =>

    na(value) ? "n/a" : levelNumberText(levelSigFig(value, sigFigs), "#.########")

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Absolute Money Text Formatter
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────

// @function Formats an absolute money value rounded to two decimals.
// @param absValue Absolute money value.
// @returns Formatted money text without a sign or currency symbol.
export levelAbsMoneyText(float absValue) =>
    if na(absValue)
        "n/a"
    else
        float rounded = math.round(absValue * 100.0) / 100.0
        rounded == 0.0 ? "0" : levelNumberText(rounded, "#.##")

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Absolute Percent Text Formatter
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────

// @function Formats an absolute percent value rounded to two decimals.
// @param absValue Absolute percent value.
// @returns Formatted percent text without a sign or percent symbol.
export levelAbsPctText(float absValue) =>
    if na(absValue)
        "n/a"
    else
        float rounded = math.round(absValue * 100.0) / 100.0
        rounded == 0.0 ? "0" : levelNumberText(rounded, "#.##")

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Money Difference Text Formatter
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────

// @function Formats current-price minus level as a signed money difference.
// @param currentPrice Current/reference price.
// @param level Level price.
// @returns Signed money-difference text.
export levelMoneyChangeText(
     float currentPrice,
     float level) =>

    if na(currentPrice) or na(level)
        "n/a"
    else
        float delta = currentPrice - level
        string sign = delta < 0.0 ? "-" : ""
        sign + "$" + levelAbsMoneyText(math.abs(delta))

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Percent Difference Text Formatter
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────

// @function Formats current-price minus level as a signed percent difference.
// @param currentPrice Current/reference price.
// @param level Level price.
// @returns Signed percent-difference text.
export levelPctChangeText(
     float currentPrice,
     float level) =>

    if na(currentPrice) or na(level) or level == 0.0
        "n/a"
    else
        float pct = ((currentPrice - level) / level) * 100.0
        string sign = pct < 0.0 ? "-" : ""
        sign + levelAbsPctText(math.abs(pct)) + "%"

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Example Usage
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Example:
//
// string priceTxt = LVL.levelPriceText(close, 5)
// string diffTxt = LVL.levelMoneyChangeText(close, prevHigh)
// string pctTxt = LVL.levelPctChangeText(close, prevHigh)
//
// ==============================================================================================
// 🔴 END REGION: Text Formatting Helpers
// ==============================================================================================


// ==============================================================================================
// 🟢 REGION: Level Label Text Helpers
// ==============================================================================================
//
// 📌 PURPOSE:
//     Provides reusable right-side level label text assembly.
//
// 🧠 USER-FACING MODEL:
//     The calling script decides which rows are enabled. This helper only assembles the
//     final padded label block in the standard MYNAMEISBRANDON level-label format.
//

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Standard Level Label Text Builder
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────

// @function Builds a padded right-side level label text block.
// @param tag Bottom-row level tag, such as [HOD], [PCL], D[1]Hi, or W[2]CL.
// @param level Level price.
// @param currentPrice Current/reference price used for difference rows.
// @param pad EM-space padding count.
// @param showPrice Whether to show the price row.
// @param showMoneyDiff Whether to show the $ difference row.
// @param showPctDiff Whether to show the % difference row.
// @param sigFigs Significant figures used for the price row.
// @returns Final multiline label text.
export levelLabelText(
     string tag,
     float level,
     float currentPrice,
     int pad,
     bool showPrice,
     bool showMoneyDiff,
     bool showPctDiff,
     simple int sigFigs) =>

    string sp = levelSpacer(pad)
    string txt = ""

    if showPrice
        txt += sp + levelPriceText(level, sigFigs) + "\n"
    if showMoneyDiff
        txt += sp + levelMoneyChangeText(currentPrice, level) + "\n"
    if showPctDiff
        txt += sp + levelPctChangeText(currentPrice, level) + "\n"

    txt + sp + tag

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Example Usage
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Example:
//
// string lblTxt = LVL.levelLabelText(
//      "D[1]Hi",
//      prevDayHigh,
//      close,
//      12,
//      true,
//      true,
//      true,
//      5)
//
// ==============================================================================================
// 🔴 END REGION: Level Label Text Helpers
// ==============================================================================================


// ==============================================================================================
// 🟢 REGION: Object Sync Helpers
// ==============================================================================================
//
// 📌 PURPOSE:
//     Provides reusable live object lifecycle managers for horizontal bar-time level lines
//     and transparent right-side text labels.
//
// 🧠 USER-FACING MODEL:
//     These helpers create an object when enabled, update it in place while enabled,
//     and delete it when the caller's visibility condition turns false.
//

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Transparent Right-Side Text Label Manager
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────

// @function Creates, updates, or deletes a transparent right-side text label at bar_index.
// @param lbl Existing label reference.
// @param show Whether the label should exist.
// @param y Label y price.
// @param txt Label text.
// @param txtColor Label text color.
// @param sizeIn Label size string.
// @returns Updated label reference.
export syncTextLabel(
     label lbl,
     bool show,
     float y,
     string txt,
     color txtColor,
     simple string sizeIn) =>

    label out = lbl

    if not show or na(y) or txt == ""
        if not na(out)
            label.delete(out)
        out := na
    else
        string resolvedSize = levelLabelSize(sizeIn)

        if na(out)
            out := label.new(
                 x=bar_index,
                 y=y,
                 xloc=xloc.bar_index,
                 yloc=yloc.price,
                 text=txt,
                 style=label.style_label_left,
                 color=color.new(color.black, 100),
                 textcolor=txtColor,
                 textalign=text.align_center,
                 size=resolvedSize)
        else
            label.set_x(out, bar_index)
            label.set_y(out, y)
            label.set_text(out, txt)
            label.set_style(out, label.style_label_left)
            label.set_color(out, color.new(color.black, 100))
            label.set_textcolor(out, txtColor)
            label.set_textalign(out, text.align_center)
            label.set_size(out, resolvedSize)

    out

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Bar-Time Horizontal Level Line Manager
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────

// @function Creates, updates, or deletes a horizontal level line using xloc.bar_time.
// @param ln Existing line reference.
// @param show Whether the line should exist.
// @param t1 Start time.
// @param t2 End time.
// @param y Level price.
// @param lineColor Line color.
// @param lineWidth Line width.
// @param styleIn Line style string.
// @returns Updated line reference.
export syncBarTimeLevelLine(
     line ln,
     bool show,
     int t1,
     int t2,
     float y,
     color lineColor,
     int lineWidth,
     simple string styleIn) =>

    line out = ln

    if not show or na(y) or na(t1) or na(t2)
        if not na(out)
            line.delete(out)
        out := na
    else
        int t2Final = math.max(t2, t1 + 1)
        string resolvedStyle = levelLineStyle(styleIn)

        if na(out)
            out := line.new(
                 x1=t1,
                 y1=y,
                 x2=t2Final,
                 y2=y,
                 xloc=xloc.bar_time,
                 extend=extend.none,
                 color=lineColor,
                 width=lineWidth,
                 style=resolvedStyle)
        else
            line.set_xloc(out, t1, t2Final, xloc.bar_time)
            line.set_y1(out, y)
            line.set_y2(out, y)
            line.set_color(out, lineColor)
            line.set_width(out, lineWidth)
            line.set_style(out, resolvedStyle)

    out

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Example Usage
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Example:
//
// levelLine := LVL.syncBarTimeLevelLine(
//      levelLine,
//      showLevel,
//      levelStartTime,
//      time,
//      levelPrice,
//      levelColor,
//      2,
//      "Dotted")
//
// levelLabel := LVL.syncTextLabel(
//      levelLabel,
//      showLabel,
//      levelPrice,
//      lblTxt,
//      levelColor,
//      "Normal")
//
// ==============================================================================================
// 🔴 END REGION: Object Sync Helpers
// ==============================================================================================


// ==============================================================================================
// 🟢 REGION: Slot Array Helpers
// ==============================================================================================
//
// 📌 PURPOSE:
//     Provides reusable synchronized object slot helpers for scripts with many repeated
//     level lines and right-side labels.
//
// 🧠 USER-FACING MODEL:
//     Instead of declaring one variable for every level line/label, scripts can keep line and
//     label arrays and update fixed slot indexes.
//
// 📎 NOTES:
//     • The slot array stores live Pine object references.
//     • Missing slots are automatically expanded with na objects.
//     • These helpers return true after updating the slot.
//

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Internal Slot Ensure Helpers
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────

_ensureLineSlot(array<line> lines, int slot) =>
    int safeSlot = math.max(slot, 0)

    while array.size(lines) <= safeSlot
        line emptyLine = na
        array.push(lines, emptyLine)

    safeSlot

_ensureLabelSlot(array<label> labels, int slot) =>
    int safeSlot = math.max(slot, 0)

    while array.size(labels) <= safeSlot
        label emptyLabel = na
        array.push(labels, emptyLabel)

    safeSlot

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Line Slot Sync Helper
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────

// @function Creates, updates, or deletes a bar-time level line stored in a fixed array slot.
// @param lines Line array.
// @param slot Slot index.
// @param show Whether the line should exist.
// @param t1 Start time.
// @param t2 End time.
// @param y Level price.
// @param lineColor Line color.
// @param lineWidth Line width.
// @param styleIn Line style string.
// @returns true after updating the slot.
export syncLineSlot(
     array<line> lines,
     int slot,
     bool show,
     int t1,
     int t2,
     float y,
     color lineColor,
     int lineWidth,
     simple string styleIn) =>

    int safeSlot = _ensureLineSlot(lines, slot)
    line ln = array.get(lines, safeSlot)
    ln := syncBarTimeLevelLine(ln, show, t1, t2, y, lineColor, lineWidth, styleIn)
    array.set(lines, safeSlot, ln)

    true

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Label Slot Sync Helper
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────

// @function Creates, updates, or deletes a transparent right-side text label stored in a fixed array slot.
// @param labels Label array.
// @param slot Slot index.
// @param show Whether the label should exist.
// @param y Label y price.
// @param txt Label text.
// @param txtColor Label text color.
// @param sizeIn Label size string.
// @returns true after updating the slot.
export syncLabelSlot(
     array<label> labels,
     int slot,
     bool show,
     float y,
     string txt,
     color txtColor,
     simple string sizeIn) =>

    int safeSlot = _ensureLabelSlot(labels, slot)
    label lbl = array.get(labels, safeSlot)
    lbl := syncTextLabel(lbl, show, y, txt, txtColor, sizeIn)
    array.set(labels, safeSlot, lbl)

    true

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Example Usage
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Example:
//
// const int SLOT_HI = 0
// const int SLOT_LO = 1
// const int SLOT_CL = 2
//
// var array<line> rowLines = array.new_line(3, na)
// var array<label> rowLabels = array.new_label(3, na)
//
// LVL.syncLineSlot(rowLines, SLOT_HI, showHi, tHi, time, hiLevel, hiColor, 2, "Dotted")
// LVL.syncLabelSlot(rowLabels, SLOT_HI, showHiLabel, hiLevel, hiText, hiColor, "Normal")
//
// ==============================================================================================
// 🔴 END REGION: Slot Array Helpers
// ==============================================================================================


// ==============================================================================================
// 🟢 REGION: History Array Helpers
// ==============================================================================================
//
// 📌 PURPOSE:
//     Provides reusable pruning and lookup helpers for synchronized history arrays.
//
// 🧠 USER-FACING MODEL:
//     These helpers support scripts that store completed levels in arrays, especially
//     newest-first arrays populated with array.unshift().
//

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Basic Prune Helpers
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────

// @function Prunes a float array by popping oldest records from the end.
// @param arr Float array.
// @param maxKeep Maximum records to keep.
// @returns Current array size after pruning.
export pruneFloat(
     array<float> arr,
     int maxKeep) =>

    int keep = math.max(maxKeep, 0)

    while array.size(arr) > keep
        array.pop(arr)

    array.size(arr)

// @function Prunes an int array by popping oldest records from the end.
// @param arr Int array.
// @param maxKeep Maximum records to keep.
// @returns Current array size after pruning.
export pruneInt(
     array<int> arr,
     int maxKeep) =>

    int keep = math.max(maxKeep, 0)

    while array.size(arr) > keep
        array.pop(arr)

    array.size(arr)

// @function Prunes a line array by popping and deleting oldest records from the end.
// @param arr Line array.
// @param maxKeep Maximum records to keep.
// @returns Current array size after pruning.
export pruneLineObjects(
     array<line> arr,
     int maxKeep) =>

    int keep = math.max(maxKeep, 0)

    while array.size(arr) > keep
        line oldLine = array.pop(arr)

        if not na(oldLine)
            line.delete(oldLine)

    array.size(arr)

// @function Prunes a label array by popping and deleting oldest records from the end.
// @param arr Label array.
// @param maxKeep Maximum records to keep.
// @returns Current array size after pruning.
export pruneLabelObjects(
     array<label> arr,
     int maxKeep) =>

    int keep = math.max(maxKeep, 0)

    while array.size(arr) > keep
        label oldLabel = array.pop(arr)

        if not na(oldLabel)
            label.delete(oldLabel)

    array.size(arr)

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Synchronized Daily-Style History Prune Helper
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────

// @function Prunes synchronized high / low / high-time / low-time / window-time history arrays.
// @param highs High values.
// @param lows Low values.
// @param highTimes High source times.
// @param lowTimes Low source times.
// @param windowTimes Source window start times.
// @param maxKeep Maximum records to keep.
// @returns true after pruning.
export pruneHiLoHistory(
     array<float> highs,
     array<float> lows,
     array<int> highTimes,
     array<int> lowTimes,
     array<int> windowTimes,
     int maxKeep) =>

    pruneFloat(highs, maxKeep)
    pruneFloat(lows, maxKeep)
    pruneInt(highTimes, maxKeep)
    pruneInt(lowTimes, maxKeep)
    pruneInt(windowTimes, maxKeep)

    true

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Synchronized HLC History Prune Helper
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────

// @function Prunes synchronized high / low / close / source-time / window-time history arrays.
// @param highs High values.
// @param lows Low values.
// @param closes Close values.
// @param highTimes High source times.
// @param lowTimes Low source times.
// @param closeTimes Close source times.
// @param windowTimes Source window start times.
// @param maxKeep Maximum records to keep.
// @returns true after pruning.
export pruneHlcHistory(
     array<float> highs,
     array<float> lows,
     array<float> closes,
     array<int> highTimes,
     array<int> lowTimes,
     array<int> closeTimes,
     array<int> windowTimes,
     int maxKeep) =>

    pruneFloat(highs, maxKeep)
    pruneFloat(lows, maxKeep)
    pruneFloat(closes, maxKeep)
    pruneInt(highTimes, maxKeep)
    pruneInt(lowTimes, maxKeep)
    pruneInt(closeTimes, maxKeep)
    pruneInt(windowTimes, maxKeep)

    true

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: History Lookup Helpers
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────

// @function Returns a float history value at index, or na if unavailable.
// @param arr Float array.
// @param idx Array index.
// @returns Float value or na.
export histFloat(
     array<float> arr,
     int idx) =>

    idx >= 0 and array.size(arr) > idx ? array.get(arr, idx) : na

// @function Returns an int history value at index, or na if unavailable.
// @param arr Int array.
// @param idx Array index.
// @returns Int value or na.
export histInt(
     array<int> arr,
     int idx) =>

    idx >= 0 and array.size(arr) > idx ? array.get(arr, idx) : na

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Manual / Requested Fallback Helpers
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────

// @function Returns requestValue when available, otherwise manualValue.
// @param requestValue Requested value, often from request.security().
// @param manualValue Manual tracked value.
// @returns Requested value when available, otherwise manual value.
export requestOrManual(
     float requestValue,
     float manualValue) =>

    not na(requestValue) ? requestValue : manualValue

// @function Returns manualValue when available, otherwise requestValue.
// @param manualValue Manual tracked value.
// @param requestValue Requested value, often from request.security().
// @returns Manual value when available, otherwise requested value.
export manualOrRequest(
     float manualValue,
     float requestValue) =>

    not na(manualValue) ? manualValue : requestValue

// @function Returns a manual source time only when the matching manual value exists.
// @param manualValue Manual tracked value.
// @param times Source-time history array.
// @param idx Array index.
// @returns Matching source time or na.
export manualSourceTime(
     float manualValue,
     array<int> times,
     int idx) =>

    not na(manualValue) ? histInt(times, idx) : na

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Example Usage
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Example:
//
// array.unshift(highHistory, completedHigh)
// array.unshift(highTimeHistory, completedHighTime)
// LVL.pruneFloat(highHistory, 25)
// LVL.pruneInt(highTimeHistory, 25)
//
// float prevHigh = LVL.histFloat(highHistory, 0)
// int prevHighTime = LVL.histInt(highTimeHistory, 0)
//
// ==============================================================================================
// 🔴 END REGION: History Array Helpers
// ==============================================================================================


// ==============================================================================================
// 🟢 REGION: Source Start-Time Helpers
// ==============================================================================================
//
// 📌 PURPOSE:
//     Provides reusable start-time routing for Active Period, Source Window,
//     Source Candle, and Source Close Candle line-start models.
//
// 🧠 USER-FACING MODEL:
//     The calling script supplies the mode string and already-resolved times. This library
//     simply decides the best available start time using the expected fallback order.
//

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Source Mode Predicates
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────

_isSourceCandleMode(simple string mode) =>
    mode == "Source Candle" or mode == "Source Close Candle"

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Source Candle / Active Period Resolver
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────

// @function Resolves a start time from Source Candle / Source Close Candle or Active Period mode.
// @param mode Start mode. Expected values: "Active Period", "Source Candle", or "Source Close Candle".
// @param sourceTime Exact source candle time.
// @param activeTime Active period start time.
// @returns Resolved line start time.
export sourceLineStartTime(
     simple string mode,
     int sourceTime,
     int activeTime) =>

    _isSourceCandleMode(mode) and not na(sourceTime) ? sourceTime : activeTime

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Source Window / Source Candle / Active Period Resolver
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────

// @function Resolves a start time from Source Window, Source Candle, Source Close Candle, or Active Period mode.
// @param mode Start mode. Expected values: "Active Period", "Source Window", "Source Candle", or "Source Close Candle".
// @param windowTime Completed source window start time.
// @param sourceTime Exact source candle time.
// @param activeTime Active period start time.
// @returns Resolved line start time.
export windowSourceLineStartTime(
     simple string mode,
     int windowTime,
     int sourceTime,
     int activeTime) =>

    mode == "Source Window" and not na(windowTime) ? windowTime :
     _isSourceCandleMode(mode) ?
         (not na(sourceTime) ? sourceTime : not na(windowTime) ? windowTime : activeTime) :
     activeTime

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Example Usage
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Example:
//
// int startT = LVL.windowSourceLineStartTime(
//      in_startMode,
//      prevWindowTime,
//      prevHighSourceTime,
//      activePeriodStartTime)
//
// ==============================================================================================
// 🔴 END REGION: Source Start-Time Helpers
// ==============================================================================================


// ==============================================================================================
// 🟢 REGION: Newest-First Rolling Extreme Helpers
// ==============================================================================================
//
// 📌 PURPOSE:
//     Provides rolling highest / lowest helpers for newest-first arrays.
//
// 🧠 USER-FACING MODEL:
//     These helpers are built for arrays where index 0 is the most recent completed record.
//     A 5-record rolling high scans indexes 0 through 4 when available.
//
// 📎 NOTES:
//     • Ties keep the most recent matching record because the resolver only replaces on a
//       strictly higher or lower value.
//     • The returned index is an array index, not a bar offset.
//     • Matching source time can be returned from a synchronized int time array.
//

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Shared Newest-First Extreme Resolver
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────

_newestFirstExtreme(
     array<float> values,
     int lookback,
     bool findHighest) =>

    float best = na
    int bestIdx = na
    int maxScan = math.min(array.size(values), math.max(lookback, 0))

    if maxScan > 0
        for i = 0 to maxScan - 1
            float v = array.get(values, i)

            bool useValue =
                 not na(v) and
                 (
                     na(best) or
                     (findHighest and v > best) or
                     (not findHighest and v < best)
                 )

            if useValue
                best := v
                bestIdx := i

    [best, bestIdx]

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Highest Newest-First Resolver
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────

// @function Returns the highest value and matching array index from a newest-first array window.
// @param values Newest-first float array.
// @param lookback Number of records to scan from index 0.
// @returns Highest value, matching array index.
export highestNewestFirst(
     array<float> values,
     int lookback) =>

    _newestFirstExtreme(values, lookback, true)

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Lowest Newest-First Resolver
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────

// @function Returns the lowest value and matching array index from a newest-first array window.
// @param values Newest-first float array.
// @param lookback Number of records to scan from index 0.
// @returns Lowest value, matching array index.
export lowestNewestFirst(
     array<float> values,
     int lookback) =>

    _newestFirstExtreme(values, lookback, false)

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Highest Newest-First With Time Resolver
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────

// @function Returns the highest value, matching array index, and matching source time from newest-first arrays.
// @param values Newest-first float array.
// @param times Synchronized newest-first int time array.
// @param lookback Number of records to scan from index 0.
// @returns Highest value, matching array index, matching source time.
export highestNewestFirstWithTime(
     array<float> values,
     array<int> times,
     int lookback) =>

    [best, bestIdx] = highestNewestFirst(values, lookback)
    int bestTime = not na(bestIdx) ? histInt(times, bestIdx) : na

    [best, bestIdx, bestTime]

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Lowest Newest-First With Time Resolver
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────

// @function Returns the lowest value, matching array index, and matching source time from newest-first arrays.
// @param values Newest-first float array.
// @param times Synchronized newest-first int time array.
// @param lookback Number of records to scan from index 0.
// @returns Lowest value, matching array index, matching source time.
export lowestNewestFirstWithTime(
     array<float> values,
     array<int> times,
     int lookback) =>

    [best, bestIdx] = lowestNewestFirst(values, lookback)
    int bestTime = not na(bestIdx) ? histInt(times, bestIdx) : na

    [best, bestIdx, bestTime]

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Example Usage
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Example:
//
// // Newest-first arrays populated with array.unshift().
// [roll5High, roll5HighIdx, roll5HighTime] = LVL.highestNewestFirstWithTime(
//      dailyHighHistory,
//      dailyHighTimeHistory,
//      5)
//
// [roll5Low, roll5LowIdx, roll5LowTime] = LVL.lowestNewestFirstWithTime(
//      dailyLowHistory,
//      dailyLowTimeHistory,
//      5)
//
// ==============================================================================================
// 🔴 END REGION: Newest-First Rolling Extreme Helpers
// ==============================================================================================
